The following are the five errors in the code snippet and their suggested solutions:

1. **The variable `i` is not declared:** All variables must be declared in C and C++ programming languages before use. The `i` variable in the for-loop must be declared beforehand as type `int`.
_Solution:_ `int i;` should be included before the for-loop.

2. **The for-loop contains a semicolon at the end:**  The semicolon `;` placed immediately after the for-loop will cause the loop's body to be empty. 
_Solution:_ The semicolon at the end of `for (i=0; i<50; i++);` should be removed.

3. **The loop body is not within a pair of curly braces:** Without curly braces indicating the body of the loop, only the statement following the loop will be executed as part of the loop body. 
_Solution:_ Enclose the statements of the for-loop's body within curly braces `{}`.

4. **The variable `total` is not initialized before use:** Before using variable `total`, it should be initialized to some value, in our case to 0 as it is going to be used to store the summation of some numbers otherwise, it could contain any garbage value and give an incorrect answer.
_Solution:_ Initialize the `total` variable to 0, i.e., `int total = 0;`.

5. **The calculation of `total` is placed outside of the loop body:** The statement that calculates the total, `total += i;` is placed outside of the for-loop. This would cause the final value of `i` (in this case, 50) to be added only once to `total`.
_Solution:_ The statement `total += i;` should be placed within the for-loop, enclosed within curly braces.

Here is the corrected code:
```C
int total= 0;
int i;
for (i=0; i<50; i++)
{
    total += i;
}
```

Below is an example code snippet to create a 'Matrix'-themed text page with green 0/1 falling endlessly.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Matrix Themed Page</title>
	<style type="text/css">
		body {
			background-color: black;
			overflow: hidden;
		}

		.matrix-text {
			font-family: monospace;
			color: green;
			position: absolute;
			font-size: 2em;
			pointer-events: none;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="matrix-text"></div>

	<script>
		const text = '01101000 01100101 01101100 01101100 01101111 00101100 00100000 01110111 01101111 01110010 01101100 01100100 00100001 ';
		let index = 0;
		const speed = 50;
		let matrixTextElement = document.querySelector('.matrix-text');

		function startAnimation() {
			let letterToDisplay = text[index];
			matrixTextElement.innerText += letterToDisplay;

			if (index < text.length - 1) {
				index++;
			} else {
				index = 0;
				matrixTextElement.innerText = '';
			}

			setTimeout(startAnimation, speed);
		}

		startAnimation();
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```

The script animates the falling green 0/1 text with the help of the `setTimeout` method, which calls the `startAnimation` function every `speed` milliseconds. The text is stored in the `text` variable and the `matrix-text` class is used to add the green color and font styling to the text. The `overflow: hidden` property of the body element hides the overflow of the text.

